GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lunaabsentcpu\fable_p1.md:13:## VERDICT: PROCEED WITH (a) — bound the walk to `d->ncpus` captured at DEVINIT (capture it AFTER the existing `ncpus > 4` exit, or clamp to `MAX_CPUS`). The batch-7 ruling survives the premise audit; the detector PLAN does not survive it as written and owes four rows (one of them mandatory) and two channel corrections.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lunaabsentcpu\fable_p1.md:47:**F9. The witness as cut already reaches M_NULLCHECK's death — through the wrong row.** After W1 survives, the probe reads SOFT_INT1 (`step_at(A_RDEV)`) -> soft bit cleared -> reassert -> else-branch -> `irqActive[1]` set -> `INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(NULL)`. But `row("soft1", "OK", ...)` is unconditional, so the log would say `soft1 OK survived` on a dead host and only C3 (`live2`) reds as BADREGS. Not vacuous (glm overstated) — a WRONG RECORD and no named channel. Add `soft1clr` (SOFT_INT1 read after W1) and `mask1clear` (MASK1=0 while the soft bit is pending) with the HALT classifier. Same for `mask1`: it checks only `g is not None` — an observation row that can never red; the detector must pin `0x00fc0000` (and pin `soft1`'s post-fix readback of 1) or (b)-shaped mutants of either arm pass.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lunaabsentcpu\fable_p1.md:70:**Q1.** No premise is wrong (F1). `interrupt_status` is one machine-wide field, software interrupts per slot; default count 1 and the rig boots with it; nothing else connects `cpu_irq[1..3]`; both arms are unbounded; four callers of `reassert_interrupts` make the corollary real, subject to F2's mask condition. Two premises the brief did not state and should: (i) W1 is lethal only because A2 armed slot 1 earlier in the SAME session (glm) — a per-row-session refactor makes `soft1` vacuously green; (ii) `step` advances every running cpu (F7).
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lunaabsentcpu\fable_p1.md:88:| **glm** (TRUNCATED mid-Q5 — file ends "on the default config of the machine"; weigh as partial) | PROCEED-(a); plan vacuous vs M_NULLCHECK/M_LATCHTHENDELIVER; readback channel disproved; corollary mask-dependent | UPHOLD (a), mask-dependence (F2), readback refutation (F5), both-calls-guard equivalence (F8), the disarm row and the second-arming row (F9, F10). OVERTURN the word "vacuous" for M_NULLCHECK — C3 reds today; the defect is a wrong-record row plus no named channel. Its member (k) is discharged by lookup's `abort()`. |
