GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\fable_adj_batch3a.md:75:- word-49 comment: `^static void row_no_lba_claim`'s comment "Setting dev_wdc.c:236 to 2 advertises LBA" — at 085766a line 236 was `d->identify_struct[2 * 49 + 1] = 0;`, the LOW byte (file convention "High byte, then low"); `= 2` gives word 0x0002, a reserved bit, not LBA (0x0200 = high byte 0x02). The CHANGELOG was corrected (#408 bullet); the detector comment was not, and it also carries a stale same-file line number. Correction: "setting the low byte `[2*49+1]` to 2 gives word 0x0002 (not LBA; LBA is 0x0200, the high byte); the row pins both bytes so either mutant reds".
