GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\fable_adj_batch3a.md:87:- `def runloop`: "*** THE `print r3` IS A COMPLETION CONTROL AND IS NOT OPTIONAL ***" — the register is printed and **no row parses it** (no `r3` reference after the driver; `row("overrun x2"` scores `"1,1,0"` counts only). A stated control that is not enforced: a `continue` that never reaches the breakpoint would be scored on the buffer, exactly as the docstring warns. RECORD plus a one-line detector repair (score `r3 = 0`).
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\fable_adj_batch3a.md:90:- fatal-call floor: `wdcflood: fatal() call sites intact` pins `grep -cE '^[[:space:]]+fatal\("'` >= 12; at HEAD it returns **13** (my comment-stripped executable census: 13 `fatal(`, 0 `exit(`, 11 `warned_*` latches, 13 guarded sites — two under `warned_badlen`, two under `warned_inbuf_overrun`, nine singles — zero `= 0` assignments; Astra's census confirmed). So a single `fatal(`->`debug(` downgrade at any one site leaves 12 and stays GREEN: the check cannot see the one-site downgrade it exists to catch, and its own text forbids the re-derivation that would fix it. Coverage debt, not a floor breach (the check is a gate row, not a fix's detector).
