GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:88:Three brief premises need correction: #337 and #341 shipped no dedicated detector; #341’s record is in `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md`; and #414’s functional fix is in `src/disk/diskimage.c`—its `dev_wdc.c` change is commentary.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:98:   The current offline gate is [gate_offline.sh](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_offline.sh), anchor `^WDCBIN=`. Relevant detector anchors are `^static void row_badlen_no_dispatch`, `^static void row_little_endian_arm`, and `^static void row_pkt_cdb_accept`. The packet row observes dispatch, not failure status. Its SCSI stub—anchor `^int diskimage_scsicommand`—returns only 0 or 1. **A regression confined to the DATA OUT return path is therefore unobserved.**
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:129:   Gate anchors are `wdc IDENTIFY: the >>24 threshold row is present` and `wdc IDENTIFY: the packing anchor is present`. The literal boundary rows detect each direct restoration of the six old modulo operations. `^static void row_anchor` supplies an independent word-53 check; `^static void row_selfconsistent` is relational, but **the whole detector is not merely a round-trip oracle**.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:137:   This commit improved the detector and comments, not executable product behavior. Its slave and capability rows remain useful; the widened cylinder sweep closes the earlier 2000-cylinder limit. #408 subsequently strengthened slave geometry checks, and #409/#410 extended identity and ATAPI coverage.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:143:   The editable gate comment still says “three rows added”; the commit added two and widened one. The detector’s capability-row comment still describes setting the low byte to 2 as advertising LBA. Its internal word value is **0x0002**, whereas the LBA bit is **0x0200**. Later corrections did not remove these surviving statements. I found no additional product defect specific to this detector-only change.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:153:   The claim that every citation in both files and CHANGELOG now names constructs is also false: old numeric citations remain in the #405 block and detector commentary. The fixture repair holds; these are record and coverage defects, not an additional live product defect introduced by this commit.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:170:   Gate anchors are `^GEOMLOG=` and `disk geometry: row failures`. In [diff_diskimage_geom.c](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/diff_diskimage_geom.c), unique anchors `override EXACT does not round up` and `override non-integral rounds up` pin the rounding boundary. There were 34 rows at shipment; the current detector has 35. Its tuples are independent expected values.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:174:   **The disclosed live narrowing remains:** an accepted 32-MiB image with H=S=1 produces **65,536 cylinders**, but WDC encodes IDENTIFY word 1 as **zero**, while its capacity remains 65,536 sectors. The detector’s cylinder sweep stops at 65,535. Retain this as the existing disclosed item.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch3a_wdc\brief_fable_adj_batch3a.md:176:   At `One-hundred-and-fifty-fourth round`, bounding H×S×512 does not bound the final cylinder multiplication against overflow; the original universal claim survives beside a later limitation. The detector comment at `honouring the override redescribes` also still says an override never resizes capacity. The final table row above disproves that generalization.
