GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch2_m88k\fable_adj_batch2.md:50:**SPLIT: yes.** The trap-like five share one fix design and one detector shape → one round `m88kexcdeliver` (HIGH). SFU1 needs FP-register modelling and is a different semantic class → separate `m88kexcsfu1` (MEDIUM). This also honours the round-scope rule (one fix design per round). The fork has already made this exact "deliver instead of halt" fix three times at the decoder layer (#302/#314/#323, CHANGELOG anchor `the fix is the one this fork has already made three times`); this is the same class one layer up, in the exception core.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch2_m88k\fable_adj_batch2.md:70:Both are **coverage debt, FILE LOW — neither is a floor breach.** Both shipped detectors clear the floor: they fail on pre-fix HEAD (clause a), fail on a verbatim reinstatement of the removed defect at the tested sites (clause b — bcnd rows for masks 0/4/f red when the table returns to NULL; the #380 taken row reds when arm 3 reverts to the plain handler), and carry independent-PC rows, not self-round-trips.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch2_m88k\fable_adj_batch2.md:116:3. **`m88kbcndm6`** — FILE, **LOW** (coverage debt). *bcnd detector has no row for mask 6; `|| m5 == 6` on the generator's NULL predicate returns a conforming encoding to `goto bad` and passes all seven rows (source-predicted, unmeasured).* Above the floor; not a breach. Rank below all live defects.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\retro_20260905\batch2_m88k\fable_adj_batch2.md:118:4. **`m88kidledup`** — FILE, **LOW** (coverage debt). *#380 idle detector cannot prove exactly-once: duplicating `ic[3].f(cpu, &ic[3])` without duplicating `slot_runs++` keeps `slot==ntn` and the idempotent store, so it escapes.* Above the floor; #381's `slot==ntn && ntp==0` already catches the counter-doubling variant. Rank below all live defects.
