GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass10_seats_20260904\fable\FINDINGS.md:62:Mask `& 0x81` keeps bit 7 (count>=8) + CEN and drops the load-variable count low bits (4–6); `0x91 & 0x81 = 0x81`, so counts 8..15 all read 0x81 — correct. **Still kills** any TxCTL-guard mutant that lands the `ovfhi` wide write: `decl` catches *any* landing (value-blind); `rb` catches CEN/bit-7 change (idata=0 clears CEN → 0x80). No landing escapes both. **No longer kills** a landed write changing only bits 1–6 while keeping bits 0,7 — but `decl` still fires, so nothing lands undetected; masking loses no landing-detection. **Control** `M_TXCTL_OVFHI = && !(reg & 0xe0)` is a plausible high-count exemption; `0x81 & 0xe0 = 0x80 != 0` → lands → rows red. It proves masking did not make them vacuous. Right control.
