web search: https://bukosek.si/hardware/collection/sgi-o2/o2-CRIME-spec.pdf
codex
The SGI table lists 28 separate 64-bit texture registers. That supports `>> 3` as a register index, but the flat `uint16_t` array needs four cells per register. I also found existing tests that compile the actual device source and inspect private state, so there is a viable detector option beyond readback or log scoring. A shift fix would also need to address alignment and bounds at the handler boundary.
